item.description:
arXiv:2609.20346v1 Announce Type: new 
Abstract: For the Dirichlet-type space $\mathcal D(\rho^{(1)},\rho^{(2)})$ on the unit bidisc $\mathbb D^2,$ where $\rho^{(1)}$ and $\rho^{(2)}$ are finite positive Borel measures on the closed unit disc $\overline{\mathbb D},$ we show that the L\'evy measure $\nu_{(\mathscr M_z,1)}$ associated with the completely alternating multisequence $\left\{\|z^\alpha\|_{\mathcal D(\rho^{(1)},\rho^{(2)})}^2 \right\}_{\alpha\in\mathbb Z_+^2}$ admits the explicit representation
  \begin{equation*}
  d\nu_{(\mathscr M_z,1)}(x)=\frac{1}{1-x_1}d((S_{*}\rho^{(1)})\times\delta_1)(x)+\frac{1}{1-x_2}d(\delta_1\times (S_{*}\rho^{(2)}))(x)
  \end{equation*} 
  on $[0,1]^2\backslash\{(1,1)\},$ where $S_{*}\rho^{(i)},$ $i=1,2$, denotes the pushforward measure of $\rho^{(i)}$ by the map $S:\overline{\mathbb D}\rightarrow [0,1]$ defined by $S(z)=|z|^2,$ $z\in \overline{\mathbb D},$ and $\delta_1$ denotes the Dirac measure at 1.
